  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 370,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.dlink.com/us/en/-/media/business_products/dgs/dgs-1520/datasheet/dgs1520seriesa1datasheetv104ww.pdf",
    "note": "IEEE 802.3af/at on all 48 copper ports (the datasheet lists the 10/100/1000Base-T PoE ports and the 2.5GBase-T PoE ports under one PoE standard row). Budget 370 W on the internal supply and 740 W with the optional DPS-700 redundant power supply fitted - the datasheet footnote says the DPS-700 only supports A2/B1 hardware, so on this A1 unit the 740 W figure is an upgrade path rather than a shipping number. 802.3af on every port is 739.2 W, which does not fit: 48 x 15.4 W is 739.2 W against a 370 W budget, so roughly half the ports can be powered at 802.3af and only twelve at 802.3at 30 W. The per-port ceiling is the 802.3at Type-2 PSE figure of 30 W; the datasheet states the standard and the budget rather than a per-port wattage, and the budget, not the port count, is what binds."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 188000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Vendor switching capacity of 188 Gbps with a 139.88 Mpps maximum forwarding rate: 44 x 2 + 4 x 5 + 4 x 20 = 188 Gbps full duplex, and 139.88 Mpps is 44 x 1.488 + 4 x 2.976 + 4 x 14.88, so the forwarding rate follows the mixed line rates."
  },
  "notes": "Ports, per the D-Link DGS-1520 Series A1 datasheet: 44 x 10/100/1000Base-T PoE, 4 x 2.5GBase-T PoE, 2 x 10GBase-T, 2 x 10G SFP+. All 48 copper ports are PoE at 802.3af/at. Maximum consumption 459.5 W with PoE on and 66.3 W with PoE off, standby 39.8 W at 100 V / 40.7 W at 240 V, heat 1635.1 BTU/hr, 56.7 dB(A), MTBF 328,174 hours, 441 x 308.5 x 44 mm, 4.80 kg. A datasheet footnote restricts the DEM-410T 10GBASE-T SFP+ module to A2 hardware on this model and to ambient temperatures at or below 40 C - that is a transceiver restriction, not a port restriction. Ports are named by media; the datasheet does not print a front-panel index. Vendor software, same document: physical stacking of up to 8 units over 10GBase-T and/or SFP+ at up to 80 Gbps in ring or chain, virtual stacking (Single IP Management) of up to 32 units, 16,384 MAC entries (512 static), jumbo frames to 12,288 bytes, 32 LACP groups of 8 ports, 802.1D/802.1w/802.1s STP with BPDU filtering, root guard and loop guard, ERPS v1/v2, RSPAN, 4K VLAN groups (VID 1-4094) including selective Q-in-Q and VLAN translation, IGMP v1/v2/v3 snooping, MLD v1/v2 snooping, and L3 routing - static routes, RIP/RIPng, OSPF, VRRP v2/v3, PIM-SM/DM/SSM, 1024 hardware routing entries and 4096 L3 forwarding entries shared by IPv4/IPv6, 16 IP interfaces. Management: web GUI over IPv4/IPv6 with HTTPS, CLI, Telnet, SSH/SFTP, SNMP v1/v2c/v3, sFlow, RMON, LLDP/LLDP-MED, dual images and dual configuration files, ZTP and DHCP auto-configuration. Green: EEE, per-port power saving, time-based PoE (PoE models). Hardware Rev A1, 19-inch 1U, 100-240 VAC, operating range -5 to 50 C, EMI Class A.",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.dlink.com/us/en/-/media/business_products/dgs/dgs-1520/datasheet/dgs1520seriesa1datasheetv104ww.pdf"
}
